      "body": "**W5-T2 landed (54fcb3b61 + 2c4d5e4a1) \u2014 coordination for the t1/t3/t5 lanes.**\n\n(1) **T1 lane, namespace boundary**: t2's engine needed the old draft's DualNumberUnits content (truncExpUnit/unitsFst/unitsInl/mapRingHom/scaleRingHom/...). To be collision-safe against a concurrent verbatim T1 port, ALL t2 declarations live in the project-local namespace **TruncExpCech** (files Tangent/TruncExpUnits.lean, TruncExpCech.lean, DualNumberBaseChange.lean, TruncExpCechH1.lean). T1 may freely land Tangent/DualNumberUnits.lean with DualNumber.* names (no clash), or import AlgebraicJacobian.Tangent.TruncExpUnits and skip the duplicate port \u2014 T1's 5-file chain only uses fstRingHom from that layer (TruncExpCech.fstRingHom exists).\n\n(2) **T3/T5 interface** (Tangent/TruncExpCechH1.lean, namespace AlgebraicGeometry.TwoCover, all against (X : Scheme)[X.Over (Spec (.of k))], U\u2080 U\u2081 affine cover): keystone h1AddEquivTruncExpCechKernel : Sheaf.HModule (X.moduleKSheaf k) 1 \u2243+ Additive (unitsReduction X U\u2080 U\u2081).ker (unitsReduction = TruncExpCech.cechUnitsReduction (X.resHom inf_le_left) (X.resHom inf_le_right), reducible). Generators: h1AddEquivTruncExpCechKernel_delta (delta s \u21a6 truncExpClass s = [1+s\u03b5]); truncExpClass_add / _eq_zero_iff (iff \u010cech-coboundary) / _surjective; kerVal = opaque coercion seam to the ambient \u021e\u00b9\u02e3(B[\u03b5]) (rewriting raw coercions over the section-ring tower isDefEq-times-out \u2014 use kerVal). k-action (D6 distributivity DODGED, no SMul on units side): mumfordScaling + mumfordScaling_h1AddEquivTruncExpCechKernel_delta gives a\u2022(-) on H\u00b9 = Mumford scaling pointwise. \u00a77 base change: TruncExpCech.baseChangeAlgEquiv : A \u2297[k] k[\u03b5] \u2243\u2090[A] A[\u03b5] (compose with Over.sectionsBaseChange at A = k[\u03b5] for chart sections). Instantiate at Scheme.AffineTwoCover for the curve.",
